Here's the modernized version using type-safe ValueTuples (requires MSTest 3.7+):

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DynamicData(nameof(TestData))]
public void Validate_ReturnsExpected(string input, bool expected)
{
    var result = Validator.IsValid(input);
    Assert.AreEqual(expected, result);
}

public static IEnumerable<(string input, bool expected)> TestData =>
[
    ("valid@email.com", true),
    ("invalid", false),
    ("", false),
];
```

**Key changes:**
- Return type changed from `IEnumerable<object[]>` to `IEnumerable<(string input, bool expected)>`
- Data uses tuple syntax `(...)` instead of array syntax `[...]`
- Named tuple elements document each parameter's purpose
- Compile-time type safety — no boxing, no runtime cast errors
